# Copyrighted material and research working files (D-25, D-28, D-29): full-text scholarly
# conversions, generated Latin dumps, copied external reference docs, and harvested dossiers
# that embed hundreds of verbatim scholar excerpts. Keep local only; regenerate with
# scripts/build_corpus_registry.py, scripts/harvest_mentions.py, scripts/build_dossiers.py.
# See HANDOVER.md s5 for what this means for a cloud session without the local corpus.
data/corpus/markdown/
data/corpus/text/
data/corpus/neoplatonism/
data/corpus/picodb/
data/texts/conclusiones_900_latin.*
docs/resources/
research-packets/
data/ontology/mentions/

# Verbatim quotations from in-copyright scholarship inside the claims layer (Ted, 2026-09-27: "don't commit anything
# copyrighted to the github"; D-29 treats per-thesis excerpt dossiers the same way). The packets, their working files,
# fix tickets (which carry the nearest source text) and the verifier sheets hold ~2,950 verbatim quotations. Keep local
# and back up privately; regenerate only by re-running the swarm. Metadata (topics, parties, scoring, links, scores,
# verdict JSON, semantic verdicts) stays tracked: it holds ids, hashes, verdicts and paraphrase, not excerpts.
data/claims/*/*.claims.json
data/claims/_work/
data/claims/tickets/
data/verification/claims/*.sample.md
data/verification/claims/targeted-*.md

# Essay fidelity sheets embed verbatim quotations: local only (D-43)
data/verification/essays/*.sheet*.md
